    "name": "SL-code-zero",
    "file": "src/systems/naval/shipLivery.js",
    "old": "  if (!Number.isInteger(n) || n <= 0 || n >= 1 << 24) return null;",
    "new": "  if (!Number.isInteger(n) || n < 0 || n >= 1 << 24) return null;",
    "tests": [
      "test/systems/naval/shiplivery.test.js"
    ],
    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "A zero's four nibbles are all none, and the door answers null for a livery of none whichever way the guard reads - so no pin can tell `n <= 0` from `n < 0`. The guard is kept because it says 'as built' before the door is asked, the way the word's other readers refuse first."
  },
